<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44341" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔχομαι</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wished for, desired</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄφρ᾽ ἔτι μᾶλλον Τρωσὶ μὲν εὐκτὰ
				γένηται</span> that <i>what they wish for</i> may happen,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.98
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δ᾽ εὐκτὰ παρὰ θεῶν ἠτησάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					843
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be wished for</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκτὸν ἀνθρώποισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					642
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				12.243
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Georg.</u>
				82
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ὁ τῶ βατράχω βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					10.52
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκτότατος γάμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					383
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκτόν ἐστι</span>
			c.inf., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				458
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.5.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>vowed, dedicated</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴουλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					10.19
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
